findings.observed:
Every question (askUntil, choose, askLineOnce) and terminalWork calls PrivateSteps.begin(). Outside a displayed result, begin() writes ESC[2J ESC[H, the title and only the remembered warnings. The encoded fingerprint is written by terminalStatus/terminalHint, or by plain console.error under NO_COLOR, and is immediately followed by that clear and the Dates prompt, with no key or pause in between. It is never readable on the alternate screen, and nothing reaches scrollback. The same redraw drops:
- the 'no MNC1 record header' info notice before the Seedshift question;
- 'Detected input format';
- the re-encode 'New backup' heading and info-kind confirmation notice;
- the Protection line, both at screen open and after re-encode's questions.
Warning-kind notices, such as the swap and cloud warnings and the re-encode fingerprint-filter warning, are retained.

